<h2>⚠️ License Expiration Warning</h2>

<p>Hi Captain {{userName}},</p>

<p>FlightJobs is sending you this email because you have enabled license expiration warnings in your profile settings.</p>

<div class="warning-box">
  <h3>Your pilot license requirements are about to expire!</h3>
  <p>You have <strong class="highlight">{{licenseCount}} requirement(s)</strong> that will expire soon.</p>
</div>

<h3>Expiring Requirements:</h3>
<ul class="list">
  {{#each licenses}}
  <li>
    <strong>{{name}}</strong><br>
    <span style="font-size: 14px; color: #94a3b8;">
      Expires: {{formatDate maturityDate}} 
      {{#if (eq daysUntilExpiry 0)}}
        <span class="text-danger">(TODAY!)</span>
      {{else}}
        ({{daysUntilExpiry}} days remaining)
      {{/if}}
    </span>
  </li>
  {{/each}}
</ul>

<div class="info-box">
  <p><strong>⚠️ Important:</strong></p>
  <p>If your pilot license expires, your next jobs will <strong>not score or pay</strong> until you renew your license. Go to your <strong>Profile → License</strong> section to check and renew your requirements.</p>
</div>

<div style="text-align: center;">
  <a href="https://flightjobs.bsite.net/profile" class="button">Go to Profile</a>
</div>

<div class="divider"></div>

<div class="info-box">
  <p><strong>🔕 Want to stop these emails?</strong></p>
  <p>You can disable license expiration warnings anytime by unchecking the box in the License popup window or visiting your profile settings.</p>
</div>

<p><em>Keep your paperwork current and fly safe!</em><br>
<strong>The FlightJobs Team</strong></p>
